<Base title={siteConfig.name} type="Home">
 <section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">A field guide to acquisition entrepreneurship</p><h1>Learn to buy a business.<br/>Understand how to fund it.</h1><p class="intro">Work through the decisions behind an acquisition: finding the right company, testing the numbers, arranging capital, and making ownership work.</p><p class="small muted spaced">Free, independent education. Practical explanations with links to the original sources.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/start-here/">New to acquisitions? Start here</a><a href="/course/">Explore the free course →</a></div></div><aside class="hero-aside"><h2>Choose your starting point</h2><ol><li><div><a href="/course/">Learn in sequence</a><p>Fourteen modules, from first principles to owning a group.</p></div></li><li><div><a href="/financing/">Follow the money</a><p>Understand debt, equity, seller terms, and their trade-offs.</p></div></li><li><div><a href="/topics/">Find a specific concept</a><p>Clear definitions, worked examples, and further reading.</p></div></li></ol></aside></section>
 <div class="stats-line"><span><strong>20</strong> course lessons</span><span><strong>44</strong> topic guides</span><span><strong>117</strong> source videos</span><span><strong>Always free</strong> no account needed</span></div>
 <section class="section" style="border-top:0"><div class="section-head"><h2>Start with the decisions that matter.</h2><a href="/topics/">Browse every topic →</a></div><div class="feature-grid"><article><p class="eyebrow">01 / The business</p><h3>What are you buying?</h3><p>Separate the company’s operating story from the seller’s pitch. Look at customers, management, earnings quality, and the work the owner actually does.</p><a href="/course/choosing-a-target/">Define a useful target →</a></article><article><p class="eyebrow">02 / The economics</p><h3>Profit is not the payment plan.</h3><p>Work from earnings to cash, then consider valuation and the timing of repayments. Keep a worked illustration separate from a lender’s actual terms.</p><a href="/course/earnings-versus-cash/">Understand the numbers →</a></article><article><p class="eyebrow">03 / The capital</p><h3>Who funds the acquisition?</h3><p>Compare the roles of a bank, equity partner, seller, or institutional lender. Understand what each contributes and what each expects in return.</p><a href="/course/building-the-capital-stack/">Read the capital stack →</a></article></div></section>
 <section class="section split"><div><p class="eyebrow">A closer look at financing</p><h2>Private credit, with the boundaries visible.</h2><p class="spaced">The first source collection discusses investor-funded non-bank lending and institutional debt. It does not establish a named, completed private-credit facility. The guide makes that distinction explicit.</p><div class="actions spaced"><a class="button secondary" href="/topics/private-credit/">Read the private-credit guide</a><a href="/course/understanding-private-credit/">Take the lesson →</a></div></div><div class="article-aside"><h2>Put examples in context</h2><p>A rate can be an illustration. A large capital amount can be a target. A promising lender conversation can remain a proposal.</p><ul class="content-list spaced"><li><a href="/examples/">Worked acquisition examples →</a></li><li><a href="/numbers/">313 numbers, each with context →</a></li><li><a href="/providers/">Firms and intermediaries: roles, not endorsements →</a></li></ul></div></section>
 <section class="section split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Read beyond the guide</p><h2>A companion to the source material.</h2></div><div><p>Our first collection brings together education from {siteConfig.collections['yusufa-sey'].name}. This site adds original explanations, comparisons, and learning paths. The videos remain the primary source.</p><p>Machine transcripts can contain errors. We flag incomplete evidence and link you back to the original material rather than presenting every practitioner statement as a settled fact.</p><div class="actions spaced"><a href="/sources/yusufa-sey/">Explore the source collection →</a><a href="/methodology/">How the material was developed</a></div></div></section>
</Base>
